      "description": "Feed enters tangentially under pressure (typically ~ 0.5–2 bar), forming an outer downward vortex and an inner upward vortex. Coarse/dense particles are thrown to the wall and leave at the apex; fines and most of the liquid leave through the vortex finder. The d50 cut size falls with smaller diameter and higher pressure; apex size controls the underflow density (avoid \"roping\").",
